name: Wave 4A — declarative domain English
description: ```
A `## Domain` section declares a kind lattice (`A deal is a kind of page.`)
with property inheritance flattened onto the subkind's struct, plus a `can
be`/`usually` enum property. Checkable-adjective definitions are registered
globally (the documented global-adjective simplification — see
IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md and the archived expressiveness report in
.ai/implementation-log-archive/docs-history/16_EXPRESSIVENESS_REPORT.md), so a definition
written against the parent kind (`page`) still applies when tested against a
subkind (`deal`) instance.

Uses `expect_swift_contains`/`expect_swift_not_contains` rather than the IR
assertions (`expect_workflow_count` etc.) — those route `MeridianTestRunner`
through its own standalone `MeridianParser`/`ASTToIR` re-parse, which does not
replicate `Compiler.compile`'s `## Domain` inline-vocabulary pre-harvest, so an
in-source-only kind lattice needs the plain compile path this spec already
exercises.
```
tags: inform7, wave4, domain, codegen

source_inline: ```
---
name: audit
parameters: deal
---

## Domain
A page is a kind of thing.
A page has a title, which is a String.
A page can be archived or live.
A page is usually live.

A deal is a kind of page.
A deal has an amount, which is Money.

Definition: a page is notable if its title is not empty.

## Phases
if the deal is notable,
  complete with reason "ok".
complete with reason "not notable".
```

expect_compile: pass
expect_swift_not_contains: _unresolved
expect_swift_contains: public struct AuditDeal: MeridianWorkflow
expect_swift_contains: public enum PagePageState: String, Hashable, Codable, Sendable
expect_swift_contains: public protocol DealKind: PageKind
expect_swift_contains: public struct Deal: DealKind
expect_swift_contains: public var title: String
expect_swift_contains: public var amount: Money
expect_swift_contains: meridianDef_Page_notable(state.get("deal"))
